A _203 _2892 @_203 fromUTF8 "^*Options:^*" @@_578 _580 I @@fromUTF8 $2684 -?                 Print usage
-a                 Clear package search path
-aPATH             Add PATH to package search path
-b64               Base64 encode the combinator code
-C                 Read and write compilation cache
-CR                Read compilation cache
-CW                Write compilation cache
-c                 Do not generate executable
-Dxxx              Pass -Dxxx to cpphs
-ddump-PASS        Debug, print AST after PASS
                   Possible passes: preproc, parse, derive, typecheck, desugar, toplevel, combinator, linked, all
-ddump-combinator-out=FILE Write combinator dump to FILE
--entry=NAME       Root and prune at value NAME (no main required);
                   with -ddump-combinator-out writes a JSON artifact
-ECMD              Set editor for :edit command
-eEXPR             Evaluate EXPR
-embed-ffis PKG*   Embed packages FFI stubs in mhs binary
-embed-packages PKG* Embed packages in mhs binary
-fno-code          Do not generate code
-F                 Run a preprocessor
-h                 Print usage
--help             Print this message
-Ixxx              Pass -Ixxx to cpphs
-iPATH             Add PATH to module search path
--interactive      Start interactive mode even with module arguments
-l                 Show every time a module is loaded
-L[FILE|PKG]       List all modules of a package
--numeric-version  Print the version number
--no-main          Do not require a main definition
-oFILE             Output to FILE
                   If FILE ends in .comb produce a combinator file
                   If FILE ends in .c produce a C file
                   Otherwise compile the combinators together with the runtime system to produce a regular executable
-optF FLAG         Pass the FLAG to the -F preprocessor
-optc OPTION       Options for the C compiler
-optl OPTION       Options passed by mhs to the C compiler for the linker
-PPKG              Build package PKG
-pFILE             Pre-load package
-pgmF CMD          Use CMD for the -F preprocessor
-Q PKG [DIR]       Install package PKG
-q                 Decrease verbosity (flag can be repeated)
-r                 Run directly
-s                 Show compilation speed in lines/s
--stdin            Use stdin in interactive system
-T                 Generate dynamic function usage statistics
-tTARGET           Select target
                   Distributed targets: unix, emscripten, windows, tcc, environment
                   Targets can be defined in mhs.conf
-v                 Increase verbosity (flag can be repeated)
--version          Print the version
-XCPP              Run cpphs on source files
-z                 Compress the combinator code
